WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.690
Wind is free.

2
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:05.390
Nobody has to dig it up,
ship it in or pay for it.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.310
And it won't run out
on any human timescale:

4
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.410
nature keeps renewing it.

5
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:17.810
Yet in 2025, fossil fuels still supplied
86 per cent of the world's total energy.

6
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.570
Solar grew by 30 per cent that year.

7
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.310
Renewables are growing
fast, but from a small base.

8
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:29.370
So if wind is free and never runs out,
why don't we get all our electricity from

9
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.310
it?

10
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.230
In this mission, you'll sort energy
sources into renewable and non-renewable.

11
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.330
Then you'll test whether a whole
country could run on wind alone.

12
00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: explain why wind can't
supply all our electricity on its own.
